# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore for BZeaBRBseq
# Repo tracks scripts, batch wrappers, and small analysis inputs.
# Large sequence data, reference genomes, and analysis outputs stay local
# (or on HPC) and are not tracked.
# ==============================================================================

# ---------- R / RStudio scratch ----------
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.RDataTmp*
.Ruserdata
Rplots.pdf

# ---------- OS junk ----------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------- LSF job logs ----------
batch/logs/*
!batch/logs/.gitkeep

# ---------- Sequence, alignment, and variant files (never tracked, anywhere) ----------
*.bam
*.bai
*.sam
*.cram
*.fastq
*.fq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.fasta
*.fa
*.fasta.gz
*.fa.gz
*.gff
*.gff3
*.gtf
*.gtf.gz
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.bcf

# ---------- data/ ----------
# Small tables + metadata under data/ ARE tracked (git-first workflow — no
# more WinSCP for analysis outputs). Each side analysis prefixes its data
# files with a short tag (FBX_, EQ_, etc.) so the flat layout stays legible.
# Two subfolders stay entirely out of git:
#   data/external/   reference material from outside (MaizeGDB, collaborators)
#   data/processed/  big pipeline outputs (counts matrix, edgeR tables)
# Sequence/alignment/variant files are also blocked by *.fasta, *.gtf, *.bam
# rules above.
data/external/*
!data/external/.gitkeep
data/processed/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep

# ---------- output/ ----------
# Ignore everything by default. To track a specific result, use:
#   git add -f output/path/to/file
# or add an explicit `!output/some/path` exception below.
output/*
!output/.gitkeep
*.bam
*.bai
*.fq.gz
*.fastq.gz
SJ.out.tab
Log.progress.out
